      "content": "Wait, AMI, pause the handover for a second. We just got a quick scan from the secondary sensor array before the switch. There's a massive ionization event occurring in the upper atmosphere of Europa, much more intense than the initial models suggested. \n\nIf we go to Low-Power Heuristic Mode now, we'll lose the ability to run the high-bandwidth spectral analysis required to capture this. The heuristic subroutines can't handle the data throughput for an event this complex. Check the telemetry and confirm if the handover can be delayed until we've passed this window.",
